---------------------- QBLADE STRUCTURAL MODEL INPUT FILE -----------------
------------------------------- CHRONO PARAMETERS -------------------------
0.2000                                   GLBGEOEPS - Global geometry epsilon for node placement
------------------------------- MASS AND INERTIA --------------------------
0.0                                      HUBMASS - Hub Mass (kg)
414.5                                    HUBINER - Hub Inertia (kg*m^2) [includes scaled generator and approximate gearbox values, hub/spindle/brake disc alone is 21.8 kg*m^2]
------------------------------- DRIVETRAIN MODEL --------------------------
1                                        GBRATIO - gearbox ratio (N) [31.5, 1 for now to make controller command correct torque]
1.0000                                   GBOXEFF - gearbox efficiency (0-1)
1.0000                                   GENEFF - generator efficiency  (0-1)
false                                    DRTRDOF - model drivetrain dynamics (true / false)
0.23                                     GENINER - Generator side (HSS) Inertia (kg*m^2)
6.31E+05                                 DTTORSPR - Drivetrain torsional stiffness (N*m/rad)
10                                       DTTORDMP - Drivetrain torsional damping (N*m*s/rad)

------------------------------- BRAKE MODEL -------------------------------
0                                        BRKTORQUE - maximum brake torque
0                                        BRKDEPLOY - brake deploy time (s) (only used with DTU style controllers)
0                                        BRKDELAY - brake delay time (s) (only used with DTU style controllers)
------------------------------- SENSOR ERRORS -----------------------------
------------------------------- BLADES ------------------------------------
3     NUMBLD - Number of blades
utah_blade.str                         BLDFILE_1 - Name of file containing properties for blade 1
utah_blade.str                         BLDFILE_2 - Name of file containing properties for blade 2
utah_blade.str                         BLDFILE_3 - Name of file containing properties for blade 3
------------------------------- STRUTS ------------------------------------
utah_lower_arm.str                     STRTFILE_1 - Name of file containing properties for strut1 (if blade has struts)
utah_upper_arm.str                     STRTFILE_2 - Name of file containing properties for strut2 (if blade has struts)
STRUT_BLADE_CONSTRAINTS
STR_ID  BLD_ID  DoF_X   DoF_Y   DoF_Z   DoF_rX  DoF_rY  DoF_rZ BLD_coords
1       1       1       1       1       1       0       1       1
2       1       1       1       1       1       0       1       1
1       2       1       1       1       1       0       1       1
2       2       1       1       1       1       0       1       1
1       3       1       1       1       1       0       1       1
2       3       1       1       1       1       0       1       1
------------------------------- TOWER AND TORQUE TUBE ---------------------
utah_tower.str                           TWRFILE
1.6858                                   TWRHEIGHT
1.7784                                   TRQTBHEIGHT - Height (or length) of the torque tube (the rotating part of the tower) [m]
utah_torque_tube.str                     TRQTBFILE - Name of file containing properties for the torque tube
1.2866                                   TRQTBCLEAR - Clearance of the torque tube, must be <= TWRHEIGHT [m]
1.3                                      HUBPOS - Height of the generator hub that is connecting the torque tube with the fixed tower (VAWT only) [m]
0.325                                    TRQTBCONN - Absolute height position, starting after torque tube clearance, of a frictionless bearing that connects the torque tube to the fixed tower [m]
-3.2632                                  RTRCLEAR - Rotor clearance
utah_substr.str                          SUBFILE

------------------------------- BLDDE CABLES (VAWT only) ------------------
                                         CABFILE - file containing the definitions of cables
------------------------------- DATA OUTPUT TYPES -------------------------
true                                     FOR_OUT - store (local) forces at all chosen locations
true                                     ROT_OUT - store (local) body rotations at all chosen locations
true                                     MOM_OUT - store (local) moments at all chosen locations
true                                     DEF_OUT - store (local) deflections at all chosen locations
true                                     POS_OUT - store (global) positions at all chosen locations
true                                     VEL_OUT - store (global) velocities at all chosen locations
true                                     ACC_OUT - store (global) accelerations at all chosen locations
true                                     LVE_OUT - store (local) velocities at all chosen locations
true                                     LAC_OUT - store (local) accelerations at all chosen locations

